@startuml recovery-class
title Fault recovery with redundancy — class diagram (SWEN-755, Group 1)

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
hide empty members

' ============ critical-service: role + recoverable state ============
package "critical-service" {

  class Main <<entry point>> {
    + {static} main(args : String[])
    ~ {static} parseRole(value : String) : ReplicaRole
  }

  class ReplicaController {
    - serviceId : String
    - role : ReplicaRole
    - lastCheckpointSeq : long = -1
    - lastHandledEpoch : long = 0
    --
    + role() : ReplicaRole
    + laneState() : LaneDepartureState
    + applyCheckpoint(cp : Checkpoint) : boolean
    + acceptPromotion(p : Promote) : boolean
    + shouldProcessSensor() : boolean
    + shouldSendHeartbeat() : boolean
  }

  class LaneDepartureState {
    - warningThreshold : int
    - consecutiveDriftCount : int
    - driftDirection : DriftDirection
    - warningActive : boolean
    --
    + apply(a : LaneAssessment) : boolean
    + apply(cp : Checkpoint) : void
    + checkpoint(serviceId, seq, sentAt) : Checkpoint
  }

  enum ReplicaRole {
    PRIMARY
    BACKUP
  }

  enum LaneAssessment {
    CENTERED
    DRIFTING_LEFT
    DRIFTING_RIGHT
  }
}

' ============ receiver: the single failover trigger ============
package "receiver" {
  class HeartbeatReceiver <<watchdog>> {
    + check() : List<ServiceStatus>
    + failoverSignals(statuses) : List<FailoverSignal>
  }
  class FailoverSignal <<record>> {
    promote : Promote
    firstAtEpoch : boolean
  }
  class ReceiverNode <<runtime>> {
    - sends Promote to backupTarget
  }
}

' ============ shared protocol: the recovery messages ============
package "protocol (shared)" <<Frame>> {
  interface Message <<sealed>>
  class Checkpoint <<record>> {
    serviceId : String
    seq : long
    sentAt : long
    consecutiveDriftCount : int
    driftDirection : DriftDirection
    warningActive : boolean
  }
  class Promote <<record>> {
    serviceId : String
    sentAt : long
    epoch : long
  }
  enum DriftDirection {
    NONE
    LEFT
    RIGHT
  }
}

Checkpoint ..|> Message
Promote ..|> Message

Main --> ReplicaController : creates
ReplicaController *--> LaneDepartureState
ReplicaController --> ReplicaRole : role
ReplicaController ..> Checkpoint : applyCheckpoint (seq filter)
ReplicaController ..> Promote : acceptPromotion (epoch filter)
LaneDepartureState --> DriftDirection
LaneDepartureState ..> LaneAssessment : apply
LaneDepartureState ..> Checkpoint : create / restore
Checkpoint --> DriftDirection

HeartbeatReceiver ..> FailoverSignal : produces on FAILED edge
FailoverSignal *--> Promote
ReceiverNode ..> Promote : encode + send (UDP)

note bottom of ReplicaController
  Backup -> primary on the first new epoch only.
  applyCheckpoint: accept newer seq for this serviceId.
  acceptPromotion: accept epoch > lastHandledEpoch
  (epoch 0 = pre-failover; first real promotion = 1).
end note

note bottom of LaneDepartureState
  The state that makes the spare "warm":
  consecutive same-direction drifts; a direction
  change resets the count to 1; warning at threshold.
  checkpoint()/apply(Checkpoint) round-trip it.
end note

note right of HeartbeatReceiver
  The only promoter. On the FAILED edge it bumps a
  per-service epoch and emits a Promote; it resends
  the same epoch while FAILED (loss tolerance, capped).
end note

@enduml
